SUMMARY:RIPA Fall Cleanup
DESCRIPTION:Join Randall’s Island Park Alliance and our Natural Areas Team for one last push to cleanup the park while the weather is still agreeable. Volunteers will not only help with picking up litter and debris but also remove invasive species\, clean walking trail paths and other duties to put us on a good path for the winter months. \nGloves\, tools and instructions included. \nAll participants must sign a Waiver of Liability. Teens aged 16 and 17 years old may volunteer without adult supervision but they must bring a waiver found at the link below\, signed by a parent or guardian. \nMinors under 16 years old must be accompanied by a parent or guardian or adult and bring the attached waiver signed by a parent or guardian. This waiver should be given to those at the registration table. \nPlease find our Liability Waiver for minors here:Community Volunteers – Randall’s Island Park \nReserve a spot here! \nLocation: Meet at Icahn Stadium \n\nFor inquiries about accessibility\, to request an accommodation\, or for event information\, please email publicprograms@randallsisland.org.
URL:https://randallsisland.org/events/ripa-fall-cleanup
LOCATION:Icahn Stadium\, East Entrance
CATEGORIES:Environmental Education,Volunteer
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/png:https://randallsisland.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/400-x-400-photos-40.png
END:VEVENT
